{
  "storyId": "B-fb7b",
  "name": "test-suite-utils-autobuild",
  "title": "Root npm test must build packages/utils before the full suite, not just packages/main",
  "description": "The root full test suite (node packages/main/dist/tasks/full-suite-runner.js, run automatically by done_required validation) fails when packages/utils/dist is absent, because sub-tests that spawn bin/lattice.js hit bootstrap-runner.js and exit with Missing build artifacts. validate.commands only auto-builds packages/main; nothing auto-builds packages/utils, so the utils build is silently required but never automated. This bit B-3783 at DONE time and recurs as the worktree-needs-utils-build pitfall. Fix: make npm test self-bootstrap by building both packages/main and packages/utils before the suite via a root pretest, closing the utils gap at the exact point utils is needed.",
  "type": "bug",
  "phase": "DEV",
  "priority": "medium",
  "keywords": [
    "build",
    "pretest",
    "utils",
    "full-suite",
    "bootstrap",
    "done-required"
  ],
